WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.689 --> 00:00:04.449
The combined method uses an initial torque followed by a specified part turn.

1
00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:05.050
First,

2
00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.289
set the wrench to 0.75 times the applicable reference torque and

3
00:00:09.289 --> 00:00:11.439
complete that first step for all bolts in the connection.

4
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:12.649
Before the second step,

5
00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:15.319
mark the position of the nut relative to the bolt threads,

6
00:00:15.649 --> 00:00:18.389
then apply the specified rotation relative to the mark.

7
00:00:18.639 --> 00:00:22.129
The required rotation depends on the total nominal connected thickness,

8
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.190
including packs and washers, compared with the bolt diameter.

9
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.610
The table gives 60,

10
00:00:26.709 --> 00:00:27.129
90,

11
00:00:27.209 --> 00:00:30.129
or 120 degrees for the stated thickness ranges.

12
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.520
Keep the table’s

13
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.840
conditions and note with the values.

14
00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:35.290
Use the marks to distinguish the completed first

15
00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:37.569
step from the required second-stage rotation.
